           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES PRICING AND AVAILABILITY FOR
         PENTIUM PRO 180MHz and 200MHz PERSONAL WORKSTATIONS


         --New Celebris XL Models Provide Workstation-class
                     Performance at PC Prices--


MAYNARD, Mass., March 12, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced immediate availability and pricing for two new 
Celebris XL personal workstations featuring Intels 180MHz and 200MHz 
Pentium Pro processors. 

     The new systems -- the Celebris XL 6180 and Celebris XL 6200 -- 
provide users of technical and compute-intensive applications a 
combination of workstation-class performance and shrink-wrapped 
applications with the look, feel, and pricing of a PC.  The Celebris 
XL 6180 and Celebris XL 6200 are priced at $5,049 and $5,249, 
respectively, and are available through Digital's resellers, 
distributors and Value Added Resellers (VARs).

     "Digital is committed to providing customers the latest in 
Intel Pentium processor technology," said Howard Elias, vice 
president, Desktop and Mobile Product Lines for Digitals Personal 
Computer Business Unit.  "Combining this processing power with 
Windows NT, and the design and reliability excellence for which 
Digital is known, make the Celebris XL the most powerful and 
affordable productivity tool available for todays serious business 
user." 

The Celebris Line:

     The Celebris XL 6180 and Celebris XL 6200 join the acclaimed 
Celebris XL line, the industry's fastest personal workstation 
family, which includes models based on Intel Pentium, Pentium Pro 
and Digital Alpha processors, as well as certain components and 
options that are interchangeable between the three platforms. 

Easy Upgrades:

     The Digital personal workstation's processor-independent 
architecture enables fast, smooth and easy migration to the latest 
Intel Pentium, Pentium Pro and Digital Alpha microprocessors, for 
long-term investment protection as customers' business needs change.  
This easy and cost-effective upgrade path from Digital -- the 
PowerGrade upgrade program -- means customers simply plug in the 
respective daughtercards to change or upgrade the processor, 
allowing them to stay on the cutting edge of performance.
 
System Configurations:

     The new Celebris XL 6180 and Celebris XL 6200 feature the 
latest high-performance versions of Intels processor and system 
logic support chip, 16MB RAM, 256KB cache, 1 GB SCSI hard drive, 
Matrox Millennium Graphics Card, and 4X CD-ROM.  In addition, 
AccelGraphics AG300 Graphics Adapters are now available for use on 
the Pentium, Pentium Pro and Alpha systems.  High-end configurations 
with 32MB RAM, and a 2GB hard disk drive, also are available.

      The systems are highly expandable and interoperate with 
management applications such as Digital's POLYCENTER, AssetWORKS, 
and ClientWORKS; Microsoft Systems Management Server; and Intel 
LANDesk Management suite for enterprise-level management.  

World Class Service and Support:

     Digital's products are backed by a three-year limited hardware 
warranty and a worldwide service and support network.  The warranty 
includes one-year of on-site service.  Digital has more than 22,000 
service professionals worldwide, including 800 Microsoft certified 
professionals, and 5,000 support professionals trained on Microsoft 
products including Windows, Windows 95, Windows NT, and a variety of 
other software products. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in todays global marketplace. 
