                       BACKGROUND FOR EDITORS       
                             March 1996


          DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION'S NETWORK SERVICES


Background

The Network Services group, part of Digital's Multivendor Customer 
Services organization, is a multivendor network systems integrator 
or VAR, providing network solutions to customers worldwide.  
Employing more than 1,300 network professionals, the group supports 
some 1,400 networking products from more than 100 vendors. Overall, 
Multivendor Customer Services has been supporting third-party 
products since 1983.
     
Network Services is one of the fastest growing segments of Digital's 
$6 billion services business.  Its growth parallels the global trend 
of network services assuming a dominant, and growing, share of the 
$185 billion worldwide IT services market. As part of Multivendor 
Customer Services, Network Services complements and leverages that 
unit's worldwide multivendor service investment and delivery 
strength across varied computing and networked environments.
     
Building on Digital's 20-year history of complex network expertise, 
Network Services offers a flexible portfolio of services for 
multivendor environments. These services all aim to help customers 
support their network's lifecycle, from planning and design to 
staging and installation to on-going support and operations 
management.
     
Services are sold through both direct and indirect sales channels.  
Since buying patterns and customer needs may differ across these 
channels, network technical specialists work closely with the sales 
forces of both Digital and its partners to help them meet these 
various needs.

Network Services: A brief look
A comprehensive service portfolio
     
     1. Planning: network strategic planning, network management 
        consulting and network technical consulting

     2. Design: network and interoperability design

     3. Implementation: project management, procurement, 
        installation, migration and update, start-up and 
        certification

     4. Management: on-site and remote systems and network 
        operations and management, network performance and capacity 
        analysis and fault diagnosis and restoration

     5. Technology Migration: NOS upgrades or migration and Windows 
        95 migration

     6. Electronic Communications: Consulting, design, and 
        implementation for Internet Service Providers and for 
        Internet client and server start up

     7. Cable TV Networks:  Consulting, design, and implemention of 
        high-speed, interactive multimedia transmission via existing 
        cable TV infrastructure

Significant multivendor skills and emphasis

     1. Training: 75 percent of training in third-party products

     2. Expertise: 
      	
     	* 2,000 Microsoft professionals (500 Windows NT/BackOffice)
      	* 300 UNIX network engineers
      	* 600 Novell-certified engineers

     3. Network integration: 50 percent of projects involve 
        third-party products

     4. Support breadth: 1,400 networking products from more than 
        100 vendors
     
A network of worldwide partners

     1. Software vendors
      	* Microsoft: 

        -- Since 1984, Digital has been a provider of support and 
        training on a broad range of Microsoft products
        -- 1995 strategic alliance calls for funding by Microsoft in
     	Digital's support and systems integration businesses focused 
        on Microsoft-based solutions. This includes training of 
        1,500 Digital Windows NT and Microsoft BackOffice certified 
        professionals
        -- 1994 agreement awarded Digital five-year exclusive 
        contract to manage the worldwide client/server 
        infrastructure for the Microsoft Network, a part of 
     	Windows 95

      	* Novell:

        -- Digital chosen as first worldwide Service Center Alliance 
        partner
     
     2. Equipment suppliers
     	
     	* Digital: Resell and integrate company's line of networking 
        products  

     	* Cisco Systems: since 1989 Digital has been a worldwide 
        reseller and support partner

      	* Bay Networks: since 1992 Digital has been a worldwide 
        reseller and US support partner

      	* 3Com: since 1991, Digital has been a worldwide sales and 
        support partner
     
A global presence

     1. 40 Network Centers serving more than 100 countries

     2. 4 interconnected Network Operations Management Centers in 
