                DIGITAL BUNDLES MICROSOFT BackOffice
                    WITH SELECTED PRIORIS SERVERS


       Provides Resellers and Customers with Industry-Leading
    Hardware and Software Server Solutions and Aggressive Pricing


MAYNARD, Mass., March 13, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it is now bundling Microsoft BackOffice server 
software with select models of Digital Prioris PC servers.  The 
Prioris BackOffice bundle provides resellers with competitive 
pricing schedules and the ability to offer customers a single source 
for the industry's leading hardware and software configurations.

     The Prioris BackOffice bundle is available for Prioris HX5166 
and Prioris ZX5133MP/2 models, which represent application and 
enterprise platforms of the Prioris product line.  The Prioris 
servers are Digital's award-winning, high-end Pentium-based 
symmetric multiprocessing computing systems that provide proven 
reliability, scalability and price/performance.  Special bundle 
pricing provides savings of up to $875.

     The Prioris HX5166 BackOffice server includes a 166MHz Pentium 
processor, 64MB ECC memory, and 4GB of PCI RAID storage at a 
suggested list  price of $17,112.  The Prioris ZX5133MP/2 
configuration includes two 133MHz Pentium processors, 2x1MB 
synchronous cache, 64MB ECC memory, and 6MB of PCI RAID storage at 
a suggested price of $24,953. A second ZX5133MP/2 configuration 
without RAID storage is also available at a suggested list price 
of $19,023.  

       Microsoft BackOffice is an integrated family of server 
software designed for installation on a single server, and is part 
of an overall architecture for both desktops and servers operating 
in a distributed computing environment.  BackOffice consists of 
Windows NT Server as the network foundation; Microsoft SQL Server 
for managing and storing data; Microsoft SNA Server for host 
connectivity; Microsoft Systems Management Server for managing PCs 
and servers; and Microsoft Mail Server, messaging software for 
information distribution.

     Microsoft BackOffice server components are designed to work 
together featuring a unified client/server architecture that shares 
a common Win32 application programming interface (API), and OLE 
component software, which greatly simplifies client/server 
applications development.

     "Bundling Microsoft BackOffice with the Prioris line is a 
natural decision and brings together two 'best-in-class' products 
to provide customers with a powerful and flexible solution for 
medium and large businesses," said Duane Dickhut, vice president of 
Digital's Prioris PC Server Product Line.  "The Prioris BackOffice 
solutions allow resellers to offer a turnkey client/sever solution 
that helps customers meet today's computing challenges and to add on 
capabilities as their needs evolve."

     Prioris BackOffice bundles are available immediately through 
Digital's channel partners, including master resellers, 
distributors, dealers, VARs and system integrators, as well as 
Digital's direct sales organizations, and are available in English, 
French and German versions, on the following systems:

     o 	Prioris HX5166 -- includes 4GB RAID storage
     o 	Prioris ZX5133MP/2 -- includes 6GB RAID storage
     o 	Prioris ZX5233MP/2 'base' -- without RAID storage or hard 
        disk to enable resellers to add their choice of storage 
        solutions
     
     All Digital Prioris PC servers include Digital's recently 
announced ServerWORKS Manager system and network management software 
and ServerWORKS Quick Launch, a CD-ROM suite of utilities that 
automates the installation of Windows NT and the configuration of 
Digital Prioris PC servers.

     All Digital's Prioris PC servers are covered by a three-year, 
on-site limited warranty, with next-business day response standard 
from Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization or a 
Digital channel partner.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
