                  DIGITAL AND SAP UNVEIL WINDOWS NT
                        AlphaServer SOLUTION


          ... First RISC Platform for R/3 on Windows NT ...


MAYNARD, Mass., and WALLDORF, Germany -- March 14, 1996 -- Digital 
Equipment Corporation and SAP AG today announced availability of 
SAP`s R/3 System on Digital`s AlphaServer family with the Microsoft 
Windows NT operating system. Together with SAP AG , Oracle Corp. and 
Microsoft Corp., Digital will provide for the first time the R/3 
business solution with Windows NT on a RISC platform. Customers can 
choose the underlying database from Oracle7 Enterprise Server or 
Microsoft SQL Server. Availability of the new solution is planned 
for mid-1996. 

     More and more customers are asking for Microsoft Windows NT for 
their R/3 projects. In October 1995 Digital announced the Prioris 
Intel based Server products for R/3. Now with the availability of 
R/3 for AlphaServer on Windows NT, Digital extends its Windows NT 
based offering from small to medium to even larger implementations. 

     While Windows NT based implementations for the Intel 
architecture offer an excellent price/performance ratio for small to 
medium sized configurations, their performance is restricted for 
large implementations. Digital AlphaServer systems with Windows NT 
break the performance boundaries because they utilize the world's 
fastest and first BIPS (billion instructions per second) 
microprocessor -- the Alpha 21164. Performance of the R/3 application 
further benefits from large memory capabilities offered only by the 
AlphaServer platform.

     "Based on Digital`s Alpha platform we can expand our market for 
even larger R/3 implementations on Windows NT. We can address new 
markets such as the thousands of OpenVMS users who were reluctant to 
move to UNIX in the past but have demonstrated a strong affinity to 
Windows NT" said Paul Wahl, SAP executive V.P. marketing and CEO of 
SAP America. 

     Digital has the broadest certified offering for SAP`s R/3 
System in the market today, including Windows NT based Intel 
solutions, Windows NT based Alpha solutions and Alpha UNIX 
solutions. 

     "Our customers now have a unique choice and a unique 
flexibility whether they prefer  Windows NT or UNIX for their R/3 
system," said Toni Steiner, Digital worldwide SAP business manager. 
"If customers decide on Windows NT they may choose our Prioris Intel 
PC server line for small to medium  requirements or Windows NT based 
Alpha solutions for medium to larger configurations. Unique is the 
ability to easily migrate to Windows NT based Alpha solutions if 
they started with PC Servers  and reach performance ceilings," he 
added. 

     For the UNIX market, Digital has demonstrated the Alpha 
performance advantage many times. Recently the company  published 
the world record (1,700 SD benchmark user for both the Oracle 
database and Software AG`s ADABAS-D) for SAP`s R/3 SD benchmark on 
Alpha systems. 

     With more than 800 R/3 installations, Digital`s service 
organization is one of SAP`s most experienced implementation 
partners. For the R/3 business the company has established SAP 
Competence Centers in many countries around the world. Based on a 
strategic alliance with Microsoft Corp., announced in August 1995, 
Digital became Microsoft`s major service provider. This relationship 
has enhanced Digital`s capabilities to meet customer demands for 
Microsoft-based solutions and support in enterprise solutions like 
SAP`s R/3 System.  

     At the CeBIT fair in Hannover, Germany, March 14-20, visitors 
can see for themselves the performance advantage of Windows NT based 
Alpha solutions for the R/3 system, either at Digital`s booth or 
SAP`s booth.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
