          DIGITAL OPENS NEW SAP PERFORMANCE TESTING CENTER


      ... Most powerful Digital technology center in Europe ...


WALLDORF, Germany -- March 14, 1996 --  Building on its strategic 
relationship with SAP AG, Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the opening of a new Digital/SAP Technology Center, where 
teams of engineers from both companies will conduct benchmarks on 
industry-specific implementations of SAP's leading R/3 solutions. 
The Technology Center is located at Digital`s offices in Viernheim, 
Germany, nearby SAP`s headquarters in Walldorf. 

     The new Digital/SAP Technology Center is equipped with seven 
AlphaServer 8000 systems with a total of 70 Alpha CPUs. Together 
with 28 GByte of main memory, 1000 GByte of disk space, and very 
fast FDDI connections, the Center provides a sophisticated environ-
ment for general and customer-related SAP R/3 benchmark tests. 

     "We are pleased to see this investment and commitment from 
Digital. The 64-bit Alpha technology is very important for SAP`s  
product development. For two years Digital has been the only 
provider of a full 64-bit operating system for our R/3 system. The 
64-bit architecture enables customers to take advantage of huge 
amounts of main memory. This is of specific interest to large 
customers that plan to implement R/3 systems with thousands of 
users," said Christa Koppe, SAP`s manager of the Digital Competence 
Center. 

     "This investment is another strong indication of the close 
Digital/SAP relationship," said Toni Steiner, Digital`s SAP 
worldwide business manager. "Customers that decide on SAP`s popular 
R/3 system want to be sure that the underlying technology supports 
their business requirements and provides smooth application growth 
as their needs grow. 

     "This is particularly true for large companies that need to 
re-engineer their business processes. They want a stable and 
long-lasting technological framework for their R/3 implementation. 
With the new Digital/SAP Technology Center, we can provide 
comprehensive SAP-related performance characterization to help 
customers estimate their platform needs," Steiner added.

     "This is Digital`s most powerful Technology Center outside the 
United States," said Klaus Steiger, technical director of the 
Digital/SAP Expertise Center in Walldorf.

Record-Breaking AlphaServer Technology

     The core of the new Digital/SAP Technology Center consists of 
Digital's top-of-the-line 64-bit AlphaServer 8000 RISC systems. 
Recently Digital announced world-record performance for SAP`s R/3 SD 
benchmark using an AlphsServer 8400 5/300 system. A joint team of 
Digital/SAP/Oracle experts measured 1,700 SD benchmark users, far 
exceeding benchmark results from any other R/3 platform providers.

     In addition, the power and quality of the AlphaServer 8400 
platform was recently demonstrated in an independent TPC-C 
benchmark. Using the world`s fastest microprocessor, the 350 MHz 
Alpha 21164, the new AlphaServer 8400 5/350 provides audited 
database performance of 11,456 transactions per minute (tpmC) at 
$268/tpmC using the Oracle7 Digital UNIX database with Oracle 64-bit 
option. 

     "This is the fastest commercial performance and best price/
performance of any server in its class and nearly twice the 
performance of the next nearest competitor," noted Pauline Nist, 
Digital vice president of the AlphaServer Business Segment. 

     Representing Digital`s database partners during the Technology 
Center opening, Fritz D|sterhaus, SAP account manager from Oracle 
Corporation, stated: "Digital`s 64-bit architecture, together with 
the Very Large Memory (VLM) option of the Oracle Database, has 
revealed significant performance increases over traditional 32-bit 
environments.  The 64-bit VLM support allows a larger portion of the 
database to reside in memory. Multi-gigabyte main memory data 
caching results in faster access to critical data and less time 
spent moving data to and from disk, thereby dramatically increasing 
application performance."

     In February, for the second consecutive year, Datamation 
Magazine recognized the quality and performance of AlphaServer 
systems by naming the AlphaServer 8400 system "1996 Readers' Choice 
Server of the Year."  After taking top honors last year with the 
AlphaServer 2100 system, the AlphaServer 8400 system is this year's 
winner, adding the coveted DATAMATION award to the system's growing 
list of accolades and benchmark records.  

     Also in February, Digital took top honors in the latest 
performance and price/performance benchmarks conducted by AIM 
Technology, a leading independent performance testing service. 
Leading the Digital list of 11 AIM Hot Iron Awards was the 
AlphaServer 8400 5/350, named best performer among multi-user/
shared systems costing $150,000 or more. 

     In the December 1995 issue of the SAPinfo Magazine, Prof. Dr. 
Hasso Plattner, vice chairman of SAP AG, said in an interview with 
UNIXopen magazine, "...We are great fans of 64-bit operating 
systems....With greater interlinking of functions, it becomes harder 
to predict who will call what, and this pushes up memory 
requirements accordingly."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
