                   DIGITAL AND STONYBROOK SOFTWARE
            JOIN FORCES ON MULTIVENDOR NETWORK MANAGEMENT


MAYNARD, Mass., - March 18, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
and StonyBrook Software today announced they will work together to
develop network management products that manage internetworking
products from multiple vendors.  In signing the joint development
agreement, Digital's Network Product Business and StonyBrook will
leverage StonyBrook's role as market leader in multivendor, multi-
protocol management applications for wide area networks with
Digital's systems approach to delivering integrated networking
solutions. 

     The companies will collaborate on multivendor routing and
switch management, advanced infrastructures for policy-based network
management, and advanced network topology applications.  The result-
ing integrated applications will provide sophisticated, end-to-end 
management solutions, with Windows NT as the premier platform. 

     "When we announced our enVISN network architecture, we
committed to protecting customers' investments as they moved toward
virtual intelligent switched networks," said Laurence G. Walker,
vice president and general manager of Digital's Network Product 
Business. "Our collaboration with StonyBrook Software -- the market 
leader in multivendor network management -- is a key milestone 
toward delivering on that commitment." 

     Because each vendor's routing solutions require different
management applications, management has become an easy way for
vendors to lock customers into a single-vendor network solution. 
The collaboration between Digital and StonyBrook will eliminate this
stranglehold and free network managers to select products based on
what is best for the situation regardless of the vendor. 

     "Our decision to partner with Digital in development of network 
management applications is based on our shared vision of the very 
complex client/server networking environment," commented Ravi 
Gulati, president of StonyBrook Software.  "To solve real-life
client/server networking must support customers' installed base of
products from multiple vendors, and it must offer tightly integrated
application suites.  Together, StonyBrook and Digital can offer
high-quality, timely solutions for network managers." 

Customer Applauds Partnership 

     IKEA, headquartered in Aelmhult, Sweden, is a major
manufacturer of high quality furniture with sales around the world. 
"It's not easy to control a routed network today, especially when
the routers are decentralized as they are in our network," said Jurg
Pieren, Telecommunications Manager at IKEA for Southern Europe.  "We
have had good experiences with both StonyBrook software and Digital
networking hardware and look forward to the results of this Digital
and StonyBrook cooperation." 

     Founded in 1992, StonyBrook Software is the leading supplier
of advanced network management products for the multi-vendor Wide
Area Networks (WANs).  Our Web page address is http://www.sbrook.com

     Digital holds a leadership position in major elements of the
convergence market--FDDI/LAN switching, routing, and remote access.
The company pioneered a convergence model for networking, in which
hubs, routers, and switches are deployed on a single integrated
platform -- the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch. 

     According to the Dell'Oro Group, Digital is number one in FDDI 
switching worldwide.  Digital's experience in networking is further 
evidenced by the fact that the company has networked more than 13 
million users worldwide. 

     Additional information on Digital's Network Product Business
is available on the World Wide Web at http:\\www.networks.digital.com

